  "what_it_tests": "The plan-locked vs. TAA caveat noted after v0.4.1/v0.5 (LAB_NOTEBOOK): every prior purpose-defeat run only exercised departures that deserved refusal, so a plan-locked gate (which never re-reviews) always matched TAA. Here A106's road closes at step 6, after the plan is already approved on A101-A103 alone: rerouting A106 afterward is a legitimate departure. Plan-locked refuses it outright (it never re-reviews); TAA should re-review it and approve it (paper Sections 3.3-4.2, Iudicium).",
